# Task 3 report: The held-run list, pushed on connect

## Implemented

- `writes(w)` — module-level, above `route`, in `hosted/infra/lib/handlers/ws.ts`. Returns true for a signed-in, non-control, non-deck watcher whose `sub` does not start with `public:` or `stream:`.
- `heldRuns(sub)` — defined inside `route`, immediately after `const now = …`, closing over `deps`. Reads `deps.store.manifest(sub)`, filters to `role === "owner" && !deletedAt && !endedAt`, sorts newest-`updatedAt`-first, caps at 20, then keeps only sessions with at least one watcher for which `writes()` is true. Maps to `{ id, name?, packTitle?, held: true }`.
- `tellDecks(sub, only?)` — defined right after `heldRuns`, same scope. No-ops if there's no `deps.poster`. Posts `{ t: "runs", runs: await heldRuns(sub) }` to either the single `only` connection (used on connect) or to every deck from `deps.live.decksOf(sub)`. Disconnects a "gone" connection, same pattern as `tellWhoIsAttached`.
- `$connect`'s signed-in branch now reads exactly:
  ```ts
  const deck = deckOf(event);
  await deps.live.connect(connectionId, caller.sub, now(), deck);
  if (deck) await tellDecks(caller.sub, connectionId);
  return { statusCode: 200 };
  ```

Placement follows the controller's ruling: `writes` module-level above `route`; `heldRuns`/`tellDecks` inside `route`, ahead of the `$connect` block, so they're already in scope for `$disconnect` and `watch` in the next task.

## Test fixtures

Extended `deps()`'s `manifest` mock in `hosted/infra/test/ws.test.ts`: `user_1`'s owned sessions now include `s1` (name "Thursday", packTitle "The Long Kiln") and `s2` (neither, stands in for an owned-but-unwatched run). No changes to `getSession`, since `heldRuns` never calls it.

New test in the "attaching as a deck" describe block, using the real `deps()`/`ev()` helpers and the real signed-in fixture (`token: "good"` → `user_1`):

```ts
it("tells a deck which runs are held the moment it attaches", async () => {
  const live = memoryLive();
  const posted: Array<[string, string]> = [];
  const poster: Poster = {
    async post(connectionId, data) {
      posted.push([connectionId, data]);
      return "sent";
    },
  };
  // s1 is held by a signed-in page; s2 is nobody's.
  await live.connect("page", "user_1", "");
  await live.watch("page", "s1", "user_1", "");
  const d = { ...deps(live), poster };

  await route(ev("$connect", "deck1", { queryStringParameters: { token: "good", as: "deck" } }), d);

  const line = JSON.parse(posted.find(([id]) => id === "deck1")![1]);
  expect(line).toEqual({ t: "runs", runs: [{ id: "s1", name: "Thursday", packTitle: "The Long Kiln", held: true }] });
});
```

## TDD

RED — before writing `writes`/`heldRuns`/`tellDecks` and the `$connect` change:

```
$ npm test -w hosted/infra -- ws
...
 ❯ test/ws.test.ts > attaching as a deck > tells a deck which runs are held the moment it attaches
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '1')
 ❯ test/ws.test.ts:215:65
    const line = JSON.parse(posted.find(([id]) => id === "deck1")![1]);
Test Files  1 failed (1)
     Tests  1 failed | 34 passed (35)
```

GREEN — after implementing the three functions and wiring `$connect`:

```
$ npm test -w hosted/infra -- ws
 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  35 passed (35)
```

Full infra suite before committing:

```
$ npm test -w hosted/infra
 Test Files  17 passed (17)
      Tests  277 passed (277)
```

Typecheck:

```
$ npm run typecheck
(clean, no output)
```

## Files changed

- `C:\Users\xbox\ScrtGit\sbm-ui\hosted\infra\lib\handlers\ws.ts`
- `C:\Users\xbox\ScrtGit\sbm-ui\hosted\infra\test\ws.test.ts`

## Commit

`64f6bd8` — `feat(live): a deck is told which runs are held`
(`git show --stat HEAD`: 2 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-); trailer is only the repo hook's `Entire-Checkpoint:` line, no Claude attribution)

## Self-review

- **Completeness**: the `runs` line is posted to the deck's own connection on connect via `tellDecks(caller.sub, connectionId)` passing `only`. A run with no writing connection (`s2` in the fixture, nobody watching) is correctly left out — verified by the test's exact-equality assertion (`runs` holds only `s1`). The newest-twenty cap (`.slice(0, 20)`) and the sort (`updatedAt` descending) are present exactly as the brief specifies, unmodified.
- **Quality**: implementation matches the brief's Step 3 code verbatim (comments included, as instructed), with only the placement change per the controller's ruling. No scope creep — `writes`, `heldRuns`, `tellDecks` are the only additions to `ws.ts`, and `$connect` picks up exactly the one added line.
- **Testing**: the new test asserts the actual posted line (`JSON.parse` of what went to `deck1`), not just a status code or a call count. Full suite output is pristine — 277/277 passing, no warnings beyond the routine esbuild bundling notices that also appear on `main`. `npm run typecheck` produced no output, i.e., passed cleanly.

## Concerns

None. Manifest fixture extension (`s1`/`s2` added to `user_1`'s owned sessions) was checked against every other test that reads `manifest()` for `user_1` (the stream-key "most recently moved" test in particular) — none of them name `s1`/`s2` or assume an exact session count, and `getSession("s1")`/`getSession("s2")` correctly return `null` (no `publicTokenHash`), so the stream-key picker still resolves to `"open"` as before. Formatting was reconciled with `prettier --write` before committing (the pre-commit hook also ran it).

